1. Portkey AI Gateway
---------------------

Source: https://github.com/Portkey-AI/gateway

Derived material:
- Request/response transforms for LLM providers, the config schema and the
  routing logic, ported from the gateway's TypeScript source.
- data/providers.json: provider parameter maps and API templates extracted
  from the gateway's provider configurations.

The gateway's main branch is licensed under the MIT License (text below).

Part of the material comes from the gateway's 2.0.0 pre-release branch (the
enterprise gateway being merged into open source). That branch's
package.json declares the MIT License, but the branch does not include a
LICENSE file, so its license terms are not stated in full. Material taken
from code that exists only on that branch:
- data/pricing/*.json: model pricing tables (copied verbatim)
- src/adapter.rs: the Messages API adapter (port of src/adapters/messages)
- src/router.rs: the circuit breaker (port of src/utils/circuitBreaker.ts)
  and sticky sessions (port of src/services/stickySessionManager.ts)
- src/analytics.rs and src/control_plane.rs: the control-plane log,
  analytics and sync formats (from src/services/winky, src/services/albus
  and the sync workers)
- src/policy.rs: usage and rate-limit rules and their error messages
- src/gateway.rs: target execution and guardrail handling, as found on that
  branch

